WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.235 --> 00:00:14.395
could not believe it.

2
00:00:15.456 --> 00:00:17.416
She was aboard the Santa Maria.

3
00:00:18.437 --> 00:00:20.697
And it was sailing away from the dock.

4
00:00:21.777 --> 00:00:23.158
"Where is Vinnie?"

5
00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:24.538
she wondered.

6
00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:27.479
Diego had disappeared too.

7
00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:30.940
Then Mandy spotted a familiar figure.

8
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.883
It was Christopher Columbus, and he was speaking with some sailors.

9
00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:38.445
"Excuse me, sir!"

10
00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:39.827
she called out.

11
00:00:41.368 --> 00:00:43.530
Mandy took the book out of her pocket.

12
00:00:44.971 --> 00:00:46.512
A sailor grabbed her arm.

13
00:00:46.532 --> 00:00:49.554
"How did you get on the ship?"

14
00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:51.176
he asked, surprised.

15
00:00:52.577 --> 00:00:54.018
"You're a little girl!"

16
00:00:54.038 --> 00:00:56.120
"Wait a minute!"

17
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.402
Christopher Columbus interrupted.

18
00:00:58.422 --> 00:01:00.964
"What do you have in your hand?"

19
00:01:03.052 --> 00:01:06.415
"This is why I'm here, sir," explained Mandy.

20
00:01:06.435 --> 00:01:09.517
"I found your book in the church.

21
00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:12.700
I knew it was important to you."

22
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.623
"I thought it was lost," Columbus said.

23
00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.806
"This must be a sign from God.

24
00:01:20.907 --> 00:01:22.928
You have brought good luck for our journey."

25
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.952
On another part of the ship, Vinnie was looking around.

26
00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:34.558
After he helped gather the spilled potatoes, Vinnie had somehow lost Mandy.

27
00:01:36.059 --> 00:01:37.881
The ship was full of activity.

28
00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:41.764
The Santa Maria was long and narrow.

29
00:01:43.225 --> 00:01:46.167
Vinnie counted more than 35 sailors aboard.

30
00:01:47.428 --> 00:01:52.973
They were uncoiling ropes, connecting equipment, and opening the large, white sails.

31
00:01:54.354 --> 00:01:57.636
Before he knew it, the ship was in open water.

32
00:01:57.656 --> 00:02:01.740
"I wonder what Mandy's doing," he thought.

33
00:02:02.976 --> 00:02:04.276
He looked behind him.

34
00:02:05.477 --> 00:02:08.298
The Niña and Pinta were following closely.

35
00:02:09.558 --> 00:02:12.299
They were smaller ships with fewer sailors.

36
00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:17.380
"Don't just stand there," said a young boy about Vinnie's age.

37
00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.701
He was holding a mop.

38
00:02:19.721 --> 00:02:22.121
"You'll get in trouble.

39
00:02:22.582 --> 00:02:23.722
Here, take this."

40
00:02:23.742 --> 00:02:27.583
"But, I'm not—," Vinnie began.

41
00:02:28.943 --> 00:02:32.228
The boy gave Vinnie an odd look.

42
00:02:32.248 --> 00:02:34.309
A big sailor walked over to them.

43
00:02:34.329 --> 00:02:37.430
"Why are you just standing there?"

44
00:02:37.931 --> 00:02:38.731
he demanded.

45
00:02:38.751 --> 00:02:40.692
"Get to work!"

46
00:02:42.452 --> 00:02:43.093
"Yes, sir!"

47
00:02:43.453 --> 00:02:44.193
cried Vinnie.

48
00:02:45.254 --> 00:02:47.414
He started mopping the deck quickly.

49
00:02:48.655 --> 00:02:49.996
The sailor walked away.

50
00:02:50.016 --> 00:02:53.997
"Thanks for the warning," Vinnie said to the boy.

51
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:57.619
"I'm Manuel," the boy said.

52
00:02:57.639 --> 00:03:00.400
"This is my first time sailing.

53
00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.041
How about you?"

54
00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:05.623
"My first time too," said Vinnie.

55
00:03:06.804 --> 00:03:09.146
Together, the boys mopped the deck.

56
00:03:10.306 --> 00:03:12.648
It was wet from the mist of the ocean waves.

57
00:03:14.029 --> 00:03:19.613
Meanwhile, Mandy stood listening as Christopher Columbus spoke to some of his crew.

58
00:03:20.994 --> 00:03:24.516
She realized that each of them had a different job.

59
00:03:26.017 --> 00:03:27.438
One man was a carpenter.

60
00:03:28.619 --> 00:03:29.840
Another was a cook.

61
00:03:31.164 --> 00:03:34.007
A silversmith and a doctor were on board too.

62
00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:39.031
"Unexpected things happen at sea," Columbus was saying.

63
00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:43.795
"Each of you has a duty to make sure this voyage is successful."

64
00:03:45.196 --> 00:03:50.140
"Any wood that needs repair, the men can see me," said the carpenter.

65
00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.664
"I'll keep the meat well salted," said the cook.

66
00:03:54.684 --> 00:04:01.369
"Captain, I'll make sure your instruments are working perfectly," said the silversmith.

67
00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:08.712
"If any men get sick or break their bones, I will take care of them," said the doctor.

68
00:04:08.732 --> 00:04:15.274
"Good. And every day, I expect a report from each of you," said Columbus.

69
00:04:15.294 --> 00:04:19.136
"Yes, Captain," the men said.
